{
  "_about": "Life-event scenarios for generate.py. Every procedure id is a MITOS id (https://mitos.gov.gr). A scenario lists the procedures a citizen may start after a life event: 'p' is the chance the citizen starts it, 'after' names scenario procedures that must have succeeded first, 'delay_days' is how long the citizen waits once it is possible (skewed towards the low end). Evidence that MITOS says a procedure requires is added automatically from the catalogue; 'evidence' overrides the chance for one evidence procedure (0 removes it). A citizen who already holds a valid result of an evidence procedure (for the validity MITOS gives, else 'evidence_validity_days') reuses it with 'reuse_evidence_probability', whichever episode or unrelated use produced it: that instance then belongs to both. 'single_use_evidence' lists procedures whose result serves one purpose only (solemn declaration, authorisation, fee). Rates, probabilities and delays are ASSUMPTIONS of this dataset, not measurements.",

